     "note": "Bands re-derive exactly from the card (af2 0.5 PROXY x/2.5 -> [0.2,1.25], gate <=1; md 129 -> [51.6,322.5]; aux 1 GUESS x/3 -> [0.3333,3]; storage 200 GUESS -> [66.67,600]), and the cited card sha256 matches; but no measurement artifact exists anywhere (out/ holds only design_args, triage_args, hashes, seals; RUN.md states \"Nothing here has run yet\"), so the anchor, 9 AF2 timings, 3 MD/aux/storage values and the 60 s sleep control were never saved.",
     "observed": "Re-derived card bands [0.2,1.25]/[51.6,322.5]/[0.3333,3]/[66.67,600] and gate <=1 match the claim exactly; re-derived measured values: none exist (0 of 9 AF2, 0 of 3 MD, 0 of 3 aux, 0 of 3 storage runs recorded)."
    },
    "findings": [
     {
      "confound": "decidability by construction: endpoints can fire both ways, but several inputs are defined by the design's own guessed reading or a substitute protocol",
      "status": "EXPLAINS",
      "crux": "The design is not forced, because every endpoint has a named refuting outcome that can occur. But Input 3 (auxiliary hours per pair) is undefined in the question and read by guess, and Input 1 may use precomputed or single-sequence alignments instead of the card's real setup. A pass would therefore decide the design's proxy question, not the card's own protocol, and the claim's scope exceeds what was tested."
     },
     {
      "confound": "Coordinates and scale: units and band width (ns/day read from the engine log, extrapolation from bytes per run to the 216-run grid, and an undefined auxiliary-hours term) could make every input land inside or outside its band regardless of the hypothesis. There are no layers or strengths in this design.",
      "status": "NEEDS_RUN",
      "crux": "The evidence contains no measured value. It holds only a pre-run design with wide bands (Input 1 spans about 6x). Refutation was named in advance, so the design is not degenerate, but nothing committed shows the unit and scale choices are sane. Those choices include precomputed alignments, a guessed 0.5 ns MD segment, linear storage scaling and the undefined auxiliary term."
     }
    ],
